                      <div id="widgetzone_CommonTabsTab1V3" class="widgetzone clearfix"><section class="widget latestinterviews clearfix" id="widgeteeecd4c4-b1ad-4008-a502-7c38272c65c7"><article class="article-size-3 interview col-xs-12">
<a href="/article.aspx?ArticleID=25417"><div class="article-title col-xs-9 col-md-8">
<h3>Advancing Mineralogy with Automated Multimodal Microscopy</h3>
<p class="hidden-sm">Eddie Hill</p>
<p class="visible-sm-block">Automated multimodal microscopy is advancing mineralogy, enabling faster mineral characterization and better mining decisions.</p>
</div>
<div class="article-thumb col-xs-3 col-md-4">
<img src="https://www.azom.com/images/Article_Thumbs/InterviewImageForArticle_25417_17840434776867376.jpg" alt="Advancing Mineralogy with Automated Multimodal Microscopy" />
</div>
</a>
</article>

<article class="article-size-3 interview col-xs-12">
<a href="/article.aspx?ArticleID=25327"><div class="article-title col-xs-9 col-md-8">
<h3>EDXRF vs. WDXRF for Slurry Analysis</h3>
<p class="hidden-sm">Tom Strombotne</p>
<p class="visible-sm-block">How EDXRF and WDXRF compare in slurry analysis, from efficiency to detection limits and solids measurement.</p>
</div>
